    "final_answer": "I'm unable to retrieve real-time agricultural data through my current tools. However, I can share some context:\n\n**Russet potato harvests** are typically reported by agricultural departments (like the USDA in the U.S.) after each growing season ends. The 2026 harvest would be reported sometime in late 2026 or early 2027.\n\nFor reference, recent Russet potato yields have generally been:\n- **U.S. average**: ~15-20 tons per acre (30-40 bushels/acre)\n- **Total U.S. production**: Varies by year, typically in the hundreds of millions of pounds\n\nIf you're looking for:\n- **Historical data** (2024 or 2025 harvests), I can try to find that\n- **Projected estimates** for 2026 based on current trends\n- **Regional breakdowns** (Washington, Idaho, etc. are major Russet producers)\n\nWould you like me to search for more specific information about a particular region or time period?"
  },
